   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Wang,<br>  Discussion of a model with orthogonal exogenous variables played a central role in the debate between Gerbing and Anderson and Fornell and Yi during the early 1990&#39;s.  It is not clear from your question what problem you are trying to solve when you say &quot;deal with&quot;.  If you want to recoup the df, you need to model the exogenous variables.  By default, lavaan will not do this.  You need to use the fixed.x=FALSE parameter which is documented in the Lavaan Options help file.  I believe that you then have to specify all covariances except the one that is zero.  I am not aware of any shortcut for that.  If desired, instead of implicitly fixing a parameter to zero by omitting it from the model specification, you can instead explicitly fix it to zero using syntax like x ~~ 0 * y where &#39;x&#39; and &#39;y&#39; are variable names.  Another common scripting trick is to include a line like &#39;x ~~ y&#39; and then comment it out so that it is there for model comparison if you need it and also as a reminder for human readers that the parameter has been omitted.<br><br>Fornell, C. &amp; Yi, Y. (1992).  Assumptions of the two-step approach to latent variable modeling.  Sociological Methods &amp; Research, 20, 291-320.  doi: 10.1177/0049124192020003003<br><br>Keith<br>------------------------<br>Keith A. Markus<br>John Jay College of Criminal Justice, CUNY<br><a href=\"http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422630749000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1O4UHxe65s1e2oAUVo-Qw-\">http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus</a><br>Frontiers of Test Validity Theory: Measurement, Causation and Meaning.<br><a href=\"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422630749000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vsLpxx68wuX-6eczEunlW\">http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/</a><br><br></div>"
    ]
